  - (an amendment attempted and WITHDRAWN, round 3) I added `.claude/active_work.md` to `scope_paths` so the handover could be updated in this branch, citing "the standing handover rule". `scope-auditor` FAILED it and was right: that rule is not documented in `working_agreement.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or `agent_guardrails.md`, and §2 requires an amendment to record CPO **authority**, not a rule name I have invented a title for. Withdrawn rather than re-argued. **The handover never needed to be in this branch at all** — the working agreement already exempts a commit touching only `.claude/task/**` and `.claude/active_work.md` from the review cycle, so it goes in its own commit. Withdrawing restored the diff to byte-identical with what all three reviewers passed (`51f6ff2…`), which is why this was not a fourth round. ⚠ THE LESSON: when a gate says a path is out of scope, the first question is whether the EDIT belongs in this branch, not how to widen the contract to admit it.
