  CPO ANSWER (conversation, 2026-08-06): **(a) confirm the amendment.** All four paths are
  authorized into this task's scope. Every one is the same edit — a sentence saying "eight" now
  says "nine", or a list gaining `.gitlab-ci.yml`. No logic, no design, nothing that changes what
  ships. The three SCOPE AMENDMENT entries above are SUPERSEDED as to authority: this ruling is the
  authority for all four, and the reviewer-FAIL footing they claim was never sufficient.

  ⚠ WHAT THE RULING DOES NOT EXCUSE, stated when granting it: these are not four independent
  extensions that each happened to be justified. They are ONE sweep that was UNDER-SCOPED WHEN THE
  CONTRACT WAS FIRST WRITTEN. All eleven restatement sites — seven on the count axis, four on the
  protected-list axis — were derivable from the routing table before the first edit. Discovering
  four of them one reviewer-FAIL at a time is the defect; the amendment is granted, the
  under-scoping is not thereby excused.

- (⭐ ROOT CAUSE, named by the CPO and filed rather than fixed here) The reason this task cost three
  review rounds is not the CI translation — that was one file and one commit. It is that the guard
  path COUNT is hand-copied as prose into SEVEN documents, and the protected-path LIST into FOUR,
  with nothing deriving either from `review_routing.json`. Changing eight to nine therefore means
  editing eleven sites, and any one missed is a document that misinforms a future reviewer. Filed
